From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Kennedy <nick@nick-kennedy.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 22:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] airconv: use public Metal atomic API for modern Xcode

DXMT v0.80 calls the private __metal_atomic_fetch_add_explicit builtin
directly. Current Metal compilers use a different private builtin signature,
so that source no longer compiles on macOS 26 / Xcode 26.

Backport the current DXMT implementation, which uses Metal's public
atomic_fetch_add_explicit API with an explicit threadgroup atomic_int cast.

---
 src/airconv/shaders/air_tessellation.metal | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/airconv/shaders/air_tessellation.metal b/src/airconv/shaders/air_tessellation.metal
index 7d0cf56..69b2e9e 100644
--- a/src/airconv/shaders/air_tessellation.metal
+++ b/src/airconv/shaders/air_tessellation.metal
@@ -150,7 +150,8 @@ struct TessMeshWorkload {
 
 int
 get_next_index(threadgroup int *out_count) {
-  return __metal_atomic_fetch_add_explicit(out_count, 1, int(memory_order_relaxed), __METAL_MEMORY_SCOPE_THREADGROUP__);
+  return atomic_fetch_add_explicit(
+      reinterpret_cast<threadgroup atomic_int *>(out_count), 1, memory_order_relaxed);
 }
 
 template <partitioning partition>
-- 
2.39.5
